  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284523/assets/ecb30a5325c08a6754af3dd1b796d55ec9446e0c93507e75db88d7745ff18dff.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(-2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1.$ For example, in the interval $(0.5,1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=1,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284523/assets/e8226d483dd0ad71d7d5e0ffae46a7e21faba7363fc266bddb52acb946c5a6a9.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(1)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (0.5,1.5).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=4.$ For example, in the interval $(3.75,4.25),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284523/assets/a43d58d99f3f72b089431ee604942f0dcbdada5ed2defac0fff6806bc9916182.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(4)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (3.75,4.25).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
